    "vulnerability": "SQL injection",
    "function": "do_login",
    "severity": "HIGH",
    "reason": "User-supplied 'user' and 'pw' values are interpolated directly into a SQL query via f-string, allowing an attacker to bypass authentication (e.g. `' OR '1'='1`) and extract arbitrary data from the database."
  },
  {
    "vulnerability": "Reflected Cross-Site Scripting (XSS)",
    "function": "do_reflect",
    "severity": "HIGH",
    "reason": "The 'name' query-parameter value is inserted into an HTML response with no encoding or sanitization, allowing an attacker to inject arbitrary JavaScript that executes in the victim's browser."
  },
  {
    "vulnerability": "OS Command Injection",
    "function": "do_ping",
    "severity": "HIGH",
    "reason": "The 'host' parameter is concatenated into a shell command string without validation or escaping, allowing an attacker to inject arbitrary commands via shell metacharacters (e.g. `; rm -rf /`)."
  },
  {
    "vulnerability": "Information Disclosure (error/query leakage)",
    "function": "do_login",
    "severity": "MEDIUM",
    "reason": "On a SQL error the handler returns the full database error message and the raw query string in the JSON response, exposing internal schema, table names, and query structure to an attacker."
  },
  {
    "vulnerability": "Sensitive Data Exposure",
    "function": "do_login",
    "severity": "MEDIUM",
    "reason": "On a successful (or injected) login the response includes the 'secret' column from the users table, leaking privileged session data or credentials that should never be returned to the client."
  }
